questions.explanation:
When two 2 port networks are connected in cascade, i.e. in a manner such that the output of the first network is the input of the next, the equivalent parameters are obtained by multiplication of their individual ABCD parameters. For Network 1, \[\begin{bmatrix}
    V_1\\I_1
\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}
    A&amp;B\\C&amp;D
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
    V_2\\-I_2
\end{bmatrix}\] For Network 2, \[\begin{bmatrix}
    V_1'\\I_1'
\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}
    A'&amp;B'\\C'&amp;D'
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
    V_2'\\-I_2'
\end{bmatrix}\] Now since \(V_2=V_1'\) and \(-I_2=I_1'\), therefore the equivalent transmission parameters include : \[\begin{bmatrix}
    V_1\\I_1
\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}
    A&amp;B\\C&amp;D
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
    A'&amp;B'\\C'&amp;D'
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
    V_2'\\-I_2'
\end{bmatrix}\] Thus, \[\begin{bmatrix}
    A_{eq}&amp;B_{eq}\\C_{eq}&amp;D_{eq}
\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}
    A&amp;B\\C&amp;D
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
    A'&amp;B'\\C'&amp;D'
\end{bmatrix}\] \[\boxed{(d)\textit{ABCD parameter matrix}}\]
